  "description": "Phase 1: process a holds a dbPessimistic Edit on the first row (30) of rows 30-32; process b begins a transaction, runs an earlier UPDATE of row 1, the multi-row UPDATE of rows 30-32 with no options, and a later UPDATE of row 50, then CommitTrans. Phase 2: a edits the last row (42) of rows 40-42; b begins, runs an UPDATE of row 2, the multi-row UPDATE of rows 40-42 with dbFailOnError and an UPDATE of row 51, then Rollback. Each statement's RecordsAffected and errors are recorded and both processes read the affected rows after each phase. Asks what a failed or partial statement leaves of the surrounding transaction.",
